## Project Name: Personal Task Manager\
\
### Overview\
The Personal Task Manager is a full-stack web application that allows users to create, organize and manage their daily tasks efficiently. The application is designed to make it easy for the user to keep track of their responsibilities and become more productive.\
\
### Requirements\
The web application should be able to:\
- Provide user authentication and authorization mechanisms.\
- Perform Basic CRUD functionality on the specified models in Python.\
- Display content in a responsive UI design with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\
- Use Django forms to create and handle the forms.\
- Handle the appropriate HTTP status codes and provide error messages for appropriate cases.\
- Allow categorization of tasks for better organization.\
- Allow the use of notes and reminders to tasks.\
- Allow the user to filter tasks by priority and category.\
\
### Technologies\
The following technologies should be used:\
- Python 3.5+\
- Django 3.2+\
- Django Rest Framework\
- JavaScript ES6\
- HTML5 & CSS3\
- Git and GitHub\
\
### Functional Requirements\
The following are the functional requirements of the application:\
1. User Authentication: Allow users to sign up, log in, and log out with email and password-based authentication.\
2. CRUD Functionality for Tasks: Creation, reading, updating, and deletion of tasks with start and due dates, notes, reminders, and priority ratings.\
3. Responsive UI: Provide an intuitive and easy-to-use UI that allows users to interact with the application with ease.\
4. Task categorization: Allow the user to categorize tasks as Personal, Work, Education, Family, and others.\
5. Sorting & Filtering: Ability to sort and filter tasks based on categories and priorities respectively.\
\
### Non-Functional Requirements\
- The application should be tested and free from bugs and errors.\
- The application should load quickly and be responsive on different devices, including mobile devices.\
- Secure login mechanism using Django's in-built authentication system.\
\
### Deployment\
The web application should be deployed on Heroku or any other suitable online platform.\
\
### Timeframe\
This web application should be completed and deployed in a maximum of 10 days.\
\
### Constraints\
- The application should use session-based authentication rather than token-based authentication.\
- The application should use Django's built-in form library.\
\
### Deliverables:\
- Fully-functional full-stack web application\
- GitHub Repository with commits\
- Documentation including installation reference, user manual, and release notes.\
\
Note that this is just a suggestion, and you can always modify specific requirements, add or remove functions, and branches as per your need. This is a valuable opportunity to show off your abilities as an essential part of this project, choose carefully, and have fun!}